    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nExtracted from https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41415\n\nPlugins cannot customize how dot-repeat applies their actions, so they do tricks like dynamically creating `<expr>` mappings, caching values, etc., which doesn't work well with mutlicursor cascade.\n\nExample:\n\n- replay/repeat a mapping that interacts with terminal-mode (`:FzfLua files`). currently not possible bc Nvim cannot know when the action \"ends\" (there is no count-verb-noun-etc grammar).\n    - plugins like fzf-lua could declare when the action ends, and how to repeat it.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nProvide `setrepeat()`.",
